WEBVTT

00:03.960 --> 00:05.400
Okay, so what is union?

00:05.440 --> 00:10.400
Union can go and return all distinct unique rows from both queries.

00:10.400 --> 00:12.680
So that means it's going to go and combine everything.

00:12.680 --> 00:16.000
And all the rows are going to be presented at the output.

00:16.000 --> 00:22.440
So since it says all distinct unique rows, that means union is going to go and remove all duplicates

00:22.480 --> 00:24.400
from the combined result sets.

00:24.440 --> 00:28.640
So union is going to make sure that each row can appear only once.

00:28.680 --> 00:29.000
Alright.

00:29.000 --> 00:31.080
So now let's have this very simple example.

00:31.080 --> 00:32.480
We have two sets of data.

00:32.480 --> 00:36.400
We have the customers where we have five customers with the first names.

00:36.400 --> 00:38.800
And as well we have another set called employees.

00:38.800 --> 00:41.360
And we have as well the first names of the employees.

00:41.360 --> 00:42.960
And we have five employees.

00:43.000 --> 00:47.960
And now if you take a look to the first names, you can see that we have the same persons as a customers

00:47.960 --> 00:49.440
and as well as employees.

00:49.440 --> 00:52.680
We have given and marry in both sets of data.

00:52.680 --> 00:54.440
So now how SQL can execute union?

00:54.440 --> 00:59.600
It's going to go and return everyone from customers and everyone from the employees.

00:59.600 --> 01:04.080
But now since we have given and married twice in the output, we're going to have them only once.

01:04.080 --> 01:05.860
So this is how the union works.

01:05.860 --> 01:09.940
It can go and return everyone from two sets, but without duplicates.

01:09.980 --> 01:14.900
Alright, so now we have the following task and it says combine the data from employees and customers

01:15.100 --> 01:16.500
into one table.

01:16.500 --> 01:20.940
So that means in one table we want to combine all informations from employees and customers.

