So now why I'm using two different semicolons because I'm telling SQL we have now two separate queries.

01:46.300 --> 01:47.980
They have nothing to do with each other.

01:48.180 --> 01:50.300
And if you go and execute it like this.

01:50.340 --> 01:52.940
And now in the output you can see we got two result grids.

01:53.180 --> 01:58.340
The first result grid is for the first query and the second one for the second query.

01:58.340 --> 02:00.260
So they have nothing to do with each other.

02:00.260 --> 02:04.660
I just want to explore those two tables in order to understand how I'm going to map those informations.

02:04.860 --> 02:08.660
So now if we check those two tables, you can see that both of them has IDs.

